---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How to Blur the Background or Edges of a Photo Online | Resize-It"
  description="Step-by-step guide on how to easily blur a photo online. Learn how to add overlay blur, blur photo edges, or create a bokeh effect without any design software."
>
  <!-- Article Header -->
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mt-[80px] md:mt-10 mb-16">
    
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="mb-8" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol class="flex items-center space-x-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Home</a></li>
        <li><span class="text-gray-400">/</span></li>
        <li><a href="/blogs" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Blog</a></li>
        <li><span class="text-gray-400">/</span></li>
        <li class="text-gray-900">Blur Photo Guide</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- Category Badge -->
    <div class="mb-6">
      <span class="px-4 py-2 bg-primary text-white text-sm font-crimson font-medium rounded-full">
        Tutorials
      </span>
    </div>

    <!-- Title -->
    <h1 class="font-crimson text-[40px] md:text-[60px] leading-tight text-gray-900 mb-6">
      How to Blur a Photo (Backgrounds, Edges & Overlays)
    </h1>

    <!-- Meta Information -->
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-gray-600 mb-8 pb-8 border-b-2 border-gray-200">
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-2">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z"></path>
        </svg>
        <span>By Resize-It Editorial Team</span>
      </div>
      <span class="text-gray-400">•</span>
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-2">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 7V3m8 4V3m-9 8h10M5 21h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"></path>
        </svg>
        <span>August 4, 2026</span>
      </div>
      <span class="text-gray-400">•</span>
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-2">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path>
        </svg>
        <span>5 min read</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Article Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700">
      
      <!-- Introduction -->
      <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-tertiary to-green-50 border-2 border-secondary/30 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Blurring an image is one of the most powerful techniques in digital design. Whether you want to censor sensitive information, draw attention to a specific subject by blurring the background, or create a beautiful aesthetic overlay for text, mastering the blur effect is essential.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-0">
          In this guide, we'll answer the question: <strong>how do you blur a photo</strong> without downloading complex apps or paying for subscriptions? We'll cover different types of blur (like Gaussian blur and edge blurring) and how to apply them instantly online.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="font-crimson text-[30px] md:text-[40px] text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6">Common Uses for Photo Blurring</h2>
      
      <p class="mb-6">
        Before we dive into the "how," let's look at why you might want to apply a blur effect to your images:
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="font-crimson text-xl text-gray-900 mb-3">1. Privacy & Security</h3>
          <p class="text-sm">Quickly obscure license plates, faces, addresses, or sensitive documents before sharing photos online. An <strong>overlay blur</strong> is perfect for hiding specific sections of an image.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="font-crimson text-xl text-gray-900 mb-3">2. Text Readability</h3>
          <p class="text-sm">If you want to place text over a busy photograph (for a hero image on a website or a YouTube thumbnail), applying a full-image blur helps the text stand out clearly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="font-crimson text-xl text-gray-900 mb-3">3. The Bokeh Effect</h3>
          <p class="text-sm">By blurring the background while keeping the main subject in focus, you simulate depth-of-field typically achieved with expensive DSLR camera lenses.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="font-crimson text-xl text-gray-900 mb-3">4. Creative Borders</h3>
          <p class="text-sm">If you need to fit a vertical photo into a square canvas, blurring the edges or the duplicated background creates a seamless, professional look.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="font-crimson text-[30px] md:text-[40px] text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6">How to Blur an Entire Photo (Overlay Blur)</h2>
      
      <p class="mb-6">
        Applying a uniform blur to an entire image is incredibly simple using our <a href="/" class="text-primary hover:underline">Image Tools</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-gray-50 border-l-4 border-primary p-6 rounded-r-xl mb-8">
        <ol class="space-y-4 list-decimal list-inside">
          <li><strong>Upload:</strong> Go to the Image Filters tool and upload your image.</li>
          <li><strong>Select Blur:</strong> Navigate to the "Blur" filter option.</li>
          <li><strong>Adjust Intensity:</strong> Use the slider to control the radius of the blur. A small radius (2-5px) softens the image, while a large radius (20px+) creates a heavy, abstracted overlay perfect for background textures.</li>
          <li><strong>Download:</strong> Click apply and save your blurred image!</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <h2 class="font-crimson text-[30px] md:text-[40px] text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6">Understanding Blur Types</h2>
      
      <p class="mb-6">
        When using advanced editors, you might encounter different types of blur. Here's what they mean:
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-4 mb-8">
        <li><strong>Gaussian Blur:</strong> The most common type. It mathematically calculates the average color of adjacent pixels to create a smooth, hazy effect.</li>
        <li><strong>Motion Blur:</strong> Blurs pixels in a specific direction (horizontal or vertical) to simulate speed or movement.</li>
        <li><strong>Radial Blur:</strong> Blurs outward from a central point, simulating a spinning camera or a zoom burst.</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- CTA Box -->
      <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-tertiary to-green-50 border-2 border-secondary/30 rounded-2xl p-8 text-center mt-12">
        <h3 class="font-crimson text-2xl md:text-3xl text-gray-900 mb-4">Ready to blur your photos?</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
          Use our free, private browser-based tools to apply beautiful effects in seconds.
        </p>
        <div class="flex justify-center">
          <a href="/" class="px-8 py-4 bg-gradient-to-br from-primary to-secondary hover:from-secondary hover:to-primary text-white rounded-xl font-crimson font-semibold text-lg transition-all duration-300 shadow-lg inline-block">
            Explore Image Tools
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
